BINANCE CREDIT TRANSACTION

In one PostgreSQL transaction:

1. Lock pending deposit
2. Confirm PENDING
3. Confirm unexpired
4. Confirm user ownership
5. Confirm verified Binance transaction
6. Confirm Binance transaction ID has never been consumed
7. Insert immutable payment record
8. Insert immutable wallet ledger credit
9. Update wallet through established wallet architecture
10. Mark deposit VERIFIED
11. Store Binance reference
12. Commit once

On any failure:

ROLL BACK EVERYTHING

Create a unique database index on Binance transaction ID.

Repeated or concurrent Verify button presses must credit once only.

Before real credit activation, run a read-only Binance test.

If external Binance eligibility, permission, or server-location restrictions block verification, fail closed and report the sanitized error. Do not fabricate a workaround.

